---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
import RangeField from '../../components/RangeField.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Back-of-the-envelope numbers" hint="What commit wait costs a write for a given clock uncertainty, how many transactions one busy row can serve, how many datacenter failures a group survives, and what the paper measured for two-phase commit and replication. A teaching model that uses the paper's own measurements where it gives them.">
  <div class="pg est" data-est>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <RangeField label="Average clock uncertainty (milliseconds)" name="e" min="1" max="20" value="4" />
      <RangeField label="Paxos commit latency (milliseconds)" name="p" min="5" max="50" value="10" />
      <RangeField label="Replicas in a Paxos group" name="n" min="1" max="9" value="5" />
      <RangeField label="Leader lease (seconds)" name="l" min="1" max="30" value="10" />
      <RangeField label="How often a leader moves its safe-time promise (seconds)" name="i" min="1" max="30" value="8" />
      <RangeField label="Groups taking part in a transaction" name="k" min="1" max="200" value="10" />
    </div>
    <dl class="est-out" data-out aria-live="polite"></dl>
    <p class="pg-note">Teaching model, with the paper's own measurements where it gives them. From the paper: uncertainty averages about 4 ms and is generally under 10 ms, the expected commit wait is at least twice the average uncertainty, Paxos latency is about 10 ms with one replica, leases default to 10 seconds and the safe-time promise is advanced every 8 seconds by default. The two-phase commit and replication figures below are the paper's measurements, on small test deployments, and are shown for the nearest case it measured; the paper did not measure other counts. Assumptions: the commit wait either overlaps the Paxos commit or adds to it (the paper's one-replica benchmark showed 10.1 ms without commit wait and 14.1 ms with it); a busy row can serve one transaction at a time because its locks are held until the commit finishes; and a group of N replicas survives losing fewer than half of them.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue, formatOneDecimalBelow100 } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-est]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = numberValue(q);
    const OUT_ROWS = 10; // lines in the result list
    const MS_PER_SECOND = 1000;
    // Table IV of the paper: two-phase commit latency in milliseconds, mean and 99th percentile, by number of participants.
    const TWO_PHASE_COMMIT: { participants: number; mean: number; p99: number }[] = [
      { participants: 1, mean: 14.6, p99: 26.55 }, { participants: 2, mean: 20.7, p99: 31.958 }, { participants: 5, mean: 23.9, p99: 46.428 },
      { participants: 10, mean: 22.8, p99: 45.931 }, { participants: 25, mean: 26.0, p99: 52.509 }, { participants: 50, mean: 33.8, p99: 62.42 },
      { participants: 100, mean: 55.9, p99: 88.859 }, { participants: 200, mean: 122.5, p99: 206.443 },
    ];
    // Table III: thousands of operations a second by number of replicas, measured with 1, 3 and 5 replicas.
    const SNAPSHOT_READS: Record<number, number> = { 1: 11.4, 3: 32.0, 5: 46.8 };
    const WRITES: Record<number, number> = { 1: 4.2, 3: 1.8, 5: 1.2 };
    const rows = Array.from({ length: OUT_ROWS }, () => { const dt = document.createElement('dt'); const dd = document.createElement('dd'); q('[data-out]').append(dt, dd); return { dt, dd }; });
    function draw() {
      ['e', 'p', 'n', 'l', 'i', 'k'].forEach((key) => (q(`[data-${key}val]`).textContent = String(val(`[data-${key}]`))));
      const epsilon = val('[data-e]'), paxos = val('[data-p]'), replicas = val('[data-n]'), lease = val('[data-l]'), promise = val('[data-i]'), participants = val('[data-k]');
      const commitWait = 2 * epsilon;
      const overlapped = Math.max(paxos, commitWait);
      const nearest = TWO_PHASE_COMMIT.reduce((best, row) => (Math.abs(row.participants - participants) < Math.abs(best.participants - participants) ? row : best));
      const measured = (table: Record<number, number>) => (replicas in table ? `${table[replicas]} thousand a second` : 'not measured (the paper tried 1, 3 and 5)');
      const data: [string, string][] = [
        ['Commit wait: twice the uncertainty (ms)', formatOneDecimalBelow100(commitWait)],
        ['Write latency if the wait overlaps the Paxos commit (ms)', formatOneDecimalBelow100(overlapped)],
        ['Write latency if the wait is added on top of the Paxos commit (ms)', formatOneDecimalBelow100(paxos + commitWait)],
        ['Most transactions a second one busy row can serve, locks held for the overlapped latency', formatOneDecimalBelow100(MS_PER_SECOND / overlapped)],
        ['Datacenter failures a group of this many replicas survives', String(Math.floor((replicas - 1) / 2))],
        ['Worst case without a leader after a leader’s zone is lost (seconds), about one lease', String(lease)],
        ['An idle group can still serve reads at timestamps at least this old (seconds)', String(promise)],
        [`Paper: two-phase commit with ${nearest.participants} participants`, `${nearest.mean} ms on average, ${formatOneDecimalBelow100(nearest.p99)} ms at the 99th percentile`],
        ['Paper: snapshot reads with this many replicas', measured(SNAPSHOT_READS)],
        ['Paper: writes with this many replicas', measured(WRITES)],
      ];
      rows.forEach((r, i) => { r.dt.textContent = data[i][0]; r.dd.textContent = data[i][1]; });
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
